13194139535897 true] [17592186373280 1104 #edb/ref 17592186373282 13194139535897 true] [17592186373280 1110 #uuid "c42f11fc-ae5d-5551-896f-cdeca7e9eb82" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373281 1034 "has the unique solution $y≡0$" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373281 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535897 true] [17592186373281 1111 #uuid "bb3e8fd3-8f3b-591f-9b29-4d40c7164892" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373282 1034 "has infinitely many solutions" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373282 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535897 true] [17592186373282 1111 #uuid "468ab820-f7f2-58a1-983d-c283f1d4decf" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373283 1034 "has no solution" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373283 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535897 true] [17592186373283 1111 #uuid "6ba4ff4e-c0af-5574-bcf0-e8fca7773130" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373284 1017 #edb/ref 17592186373285 13194139535897 true] [17592186373284 1089 "q-339297" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373284 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535897 true] [17592186373284 1100 "Consider the following boundary value problem.\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-y=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)-y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(1)-y(1)=0,\\,0\\le x\\le 1\n$$\n\nFind the solution to this boundary value problem in terms of an arbitrary constant $A.$\n\nThe solution is $y=A\\,\\cdot $\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373284 1113 #uuid "64adb40a-93af-5684-81b2-e7031fa0c08c" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373284 1145 "To solve the homogeneous boundary value problem, we first find the general solution and then determine the values of the arbitrary constants that fit the boundary conditions.\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-1 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $m=\\pm 1.$ So, the fundamental solutions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x},\\,{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=A{e}^{x}-B{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nApplying the condition ${y}^{′}(0)-y(0)=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-B-(A+B) & =0 \\\\ -2B & =0 \\\\ B & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nApplying the condition ${y}^{′}(1)-y(1)=0,$ we have\n\n$$\nA{e}^{1}-A{e}^{1}=0,\n$$\n\nwhich is automatically satisfied for any $A.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the BVP is\n\n$$\ny=A\\cdot {e}^{x},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is arbitrary." 13194139535897 true] [17592186373285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373286 13194139535897 true] [17592186373285 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535897 true] [17592186373285 1041 "field-1" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373285 1104 #edb/ref 17592186373286 13194139535897 true] [17592186373285 1110 #uuid "219f513c-861f-5db4-9983-0e9899251310" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373286 1034 "e^x" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373286 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535897 true] [17592186373286 1111 #uuid "a8f4b4d6-ec87-5e63-866d-8a598bf11a61" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373287 1017 #edb/ref 17592186373288 13194139535897 true] [17592186373287 1089 "q-339475" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373287 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535897 true] [17592186373287 1100 "Consider the following boundary value problem.\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+y=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=0,\\,y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0,\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to this boundary value problem in terms of an arbitrary constant $A.$\n\nThe solution is $y=A\\,\\cdot $\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373287 1113 #uuid "e1025e9c-a186-5c7a-9a6b-d73bfd767c22" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373287 1145 "To solve the homogeneous boundary value problem, we first find the general solution and then determine the values of the arbitrary constants that fit the boundary conditions.\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}+1 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $m=\\pm \\text{i}.$ So, the fundamental solutions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,{y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-A\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+B\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nApplying the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n-A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=0\\,⇒\\,B=0.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\ny=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nApplying the condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0,$ we have\n\n$$\nA\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0,\n$$\n\nwhich is automatically satisfied for any $A.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the BVP is $y=A\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ where $A$ is arbitrary." 13194139535897 true] [17592186373288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373289 13194139535897 true] [17592186373288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186373290 13194139535897 true] [17592186373288 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535897 true] [17592186373288 1041 "field-1" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373288 1104 #edb/ref 17592186373289 13194139535897 true] [17592186373288 1110 #uuid "ec8b1e5d-5284-578f-95d4-112672c62c00" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373289 1034 "\\cos(x)" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373289 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535897 true] [17592186373289 1111 #uuid "625b866a-0d0f-5e3c-a699-0967fcf850dc" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373290 1034 "\\sin(x)" 13194139535897 true] [17592186373290 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535897 true] [17592186373290 1111 #uuid "a83222f6-580c-5d99-8658-fc12dde43786" 13194139535897 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-338525/field-2/ma-v1/461f7cbfc6a1960526370073a405c9aaa6391e98ee7bf22921bfc65c0e2d84c2" 17592186373196 "q-338525/field-2/ma-v1/461f7cbfc6a1960526370073a405c9aaa6391e98ee7bf22921bfc65c0e2d84c2/5f6a04ebb2b04dacf40c11bd5b14b2febbc6ed33d2b0a71cbe4e1ba655bd4b1f" 17592186373197 "q-338525/field-2/ma-v1/461f7cbfc6a1960526370073a405c9aaa6391e98ee7bf22921bfc65c0e2d84c2/985badd296b7c6c04e58719e043d43ea3f095cf16a5d52fc7c81ad0484c967e0" 1759218637